= The Quarrel in the Kremlin

The reports from Germany reach Moscow before the delegates. [? if march_action = 1 : Kun's says the March Action was a step forward. Levi's letter to Lenin says it was a crime. Radek's says both, depending on the page. ?][? if march_action = 2 : Kun's says the victory in Central Germany proves the theory of the offensive. Radek's says the Reichswehr had its own reasons for staying in barracks. ?][? if march_action = 0 : Kun's says the German Zentrale let Hörsing occupy Mansfeld without firing a shot. Radek's says it kept the party alive. ?]

Zinoviev has staked his name on Kun. Lenin is angry, though it is not yet clear with whom. Before the world congress opens in June, the Zentrale can send someone ahead to Moscow.

- @lenin: Send Clara Zetkin to Lenin.
- @zinoviev: Send the Left's men to Zinoviev.
- @radek: Work through Radek.
- @wait: Send nobody.

@lenin
subtitle: Lenin will hear the truth about March. Zinoviev will know who told him.
choose-if: comrade_zetkin = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Zetkin is not free to travel.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_moscow_friend = 1;
RG.ecci('lenin', 12);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -8);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

Zetkin travels by way of Stettin and Reval. Lenin receives her in his study with a plaid over his knees and lets her talk for an hour. [? if march_action = 1 : When she has finished, he says that Levi was right about March, and that it does not excuse the way he said it. ?][? if march_action != 1 : He asks about the factory councils, and says that the German party must learn to be patient without being passive. ?]

@zinoviev
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
subtitle: Zinoviev and Bukharin are the Left's friends, and friends must be kept. Lenin will notice.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_moscow_friend = 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 8);
RG.ecci('lenin', -8);
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Frölich and two Berlin delegates go to the Hotel Lux and from there to Zinoviev's office. Zinoviev embraces them and promises to defend them at the congress. He does not say against whom.

@radek
subtitle: The middle of the Executive, and a man who changes sides on time.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_moscow_friend = 3;
RG.ecci('radek', 12);
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Thalheimer writes to Radek every other day. Radek answers with jokes and good advice, and passes the letters to Lenin when they say what Lenin wants to hear.

@wait
subtitle: The party keeps its own counsel. All five of them will take the silence as an insult.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 4;
RG.ecci('all', -3);
!}

The delegation will travel together in June and speak with one voice, if it can find one.
